---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const pages = [
  {
    href: `${base}about/site/build/`,
    title: "How it's built",
    summary: "The public hub, the private layer, the sign-in gate, and the leak checks that keep them apart.",
  },
  {
    href: `${base}about/site/use/`,
    title: "How it's used",
    summary: "What a collaborator sees after signing in: projects, calendar, notes, and single-page share links.",
  },
  {
    href: `${base}about/site/publishing/`,
    title: "How publishing works",
    summary: "From a repository push to a validated manifest, a content bucket, and a project page behind the gate.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About this site"
  description="How this research site is built, how collaborators use it, and how private work is published without leaking."
>
  <article class="about-site">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this site</p>
    <h1>One public hub, one private layer</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This site has a public face and a members-only layer behind a sign-in gate. The two are built
      from the same repository but never share an output directory. Public pages are static; private
      pages are served only after the gate has made an access decision.
    </p>

    <nav class="about-cards" aria-label="About this site">
      {
        pages.map((page) => (
          <a class="about-card" href={page.href}>
            <span class="about-card-title">{page.title}</span>
            <span class="about-card-summary">{page.summary}</span>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </nav>

    <section>
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        The public site is a static build published from this repository. The private layer is a
        second build of the same repository, uploaded to a content bucket and served through a
        Cloud Run gate that checks a Firebase session and a Firestore access policy. Research
        projects publish into that bucket as versioned manifests, so a project can be updated
        without rebuilding the hub.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three guardrails keep private work private: a styled not-found response that is identical
        whether a private page is missing or forbidden; an allowlist for what may be published to
        the public origin; and a leak check that scans every public byte for the titles, summaries,
        slugs and paths of private items.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who sees what</h2>
      <p>
        A signed-out visitor sees the public research, papers, CV and writing. Signing in does not
        open a second site: it adds Projects, Calendar and Notes to the same menu. The owner also
        sees an Admin area for members, access rules, share links and publish status.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-site {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent, #861f41);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .about-cards {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .about-cards {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .about-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border, #d8d2cc);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    background: var(--color-surface, #fff);
  }

  .about-card:hover,
  .about-card:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--color-accent, #861f41);
  }

  .about-card-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .about-card-summary {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
</style>
